WEBVTT

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone is about to start!

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.680
It's illegal to play soccer?!

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.780
What do you mean?

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.470
Unfortunately as of today, Raimon's soccer club is disbanded.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:18.100
Disbanded?

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.080
No way...

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.330
But we just got the soccer club back to normal again...

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.070
Extra! Extra!

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.080
A ban on soccer has been passed!

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.810
No! No!

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:30.760
I'm sorry.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.620
We have no choice.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.030
An uncivilized and dangerous sport! {ごめん、いつもここで吹いてしまう xD}

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.790
Soccer has been banned!

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:44.250
Everyone carrying soccer balls, uniforms, spikes, and such other items related to soccer must hand them in to be destroyed immediately!

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.170
My soccer ball!

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.660
The soccer ban...

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.360
Why does it have to be banned?

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.820
Because of the way we acted against a team from another country in that game.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.010
I guess this is only a natural consequence of what happened.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.730
That game?

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.530
What are you talking about?

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.520
The friendly between Japan and America one month ago.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:53.590
I know that one!

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.340
It was such a great game!

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.900
I watched it on TV too, while I was in Okinawa!

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.570
It was so exciting!

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.360
Yeah!

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.490
Watching it made me love soccer more than ever!

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.620
Me too!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.980
I was glued to the TV!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.550
Do you recall just as soon as it began-

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.930
You guys...

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.930
You thought that was a good game?

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.250
Are you sure you're not mistaking it for another one?

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.320
Yeah.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.350
The game got suspended because Japan's representatives were acting violently.

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.510
Suspended?

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.570
Almost all of America's team got major injuries.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.000
Even though it was only a friendly.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.940
It's a disgrace to Japan's soccer.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:38.900
That game is exactly what got everyone thinking that soccer is a dangerous and uncivilized sport.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.380
Yeah.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:45.470
It wouldn't be a far stretch to assume that the soccer ban is an outcome of that game.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:47.770
Could this be...

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.990
So that's how the soccer ban came about.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.000
It's clearly the foul work of El Dorado!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.590
There's no doubt about it.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.380
They got involved in the match between Japan and America.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.210
Really, there's just no turning our backs on them.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.080
Nice to meet you, miss.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.600
I am Clark Wonderbat.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.310
Call me Wondeba!

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.340
As expected of Protocol Omega 2.0.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.150
A job well done.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.420
Good work, Beta.

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:27.240
You are on a different level from Alpha.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.870
Why, thank you.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:37.170
That is why I, Clark Wonderbat, am not anyone suspicious!

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.760
And this is Fei.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:41.840
Hello.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:43.680
Hello...

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.510
Um, Fei-kun, are you also...?

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:46.590
Yes.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.140
I'm from the future.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.080
We're here to set right what's been changed in the past.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.290
Changed in the past...

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.500
I remember now.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.820
My past was close to being changed too.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:04.610
If soccer hadn't been protected back then, Raimon's soccer club wouldn't exist today.

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.210
Oh, man!

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.960
My head's gotten all mixed up with all this past stuff and whatnot!

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:13.950
The soccer ban is a result of the past having been changed...

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.330
Exactly!

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.450
Good job, Akane!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.760
As expected from a big science fiction fan!

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.410
Let's do a recheck.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:25.380
Do you all remember the match from one month ago?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.600
I saw it on TV.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.160
What was the result?

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.100
Japan won at 3-2.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.240
That's completely wrong!

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:36.660
I was at the stadium and saw it all for myself!

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.140
Yes.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:42.670
From my memory, the score was 10-0 by the end of the first half...

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:46.820
And the game was suspended because of extremely violent behavior from Japan's team.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:50.490
This makes it clear.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.320
A parallel world.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.130
Exactly!

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.730
What do you mean?

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:59.960
Casualties among America's national team grow by the minute!

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.330
Yes, this is it!

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:11.510
Oh dear, and another red card for Japan's national team!

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.240
What's this?

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.670
Japan's representative is ignoring the ref's call and continuing to play!

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:20.010
This is bad! This is very bad!

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.560
What a horrible game.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.020
Every time I watch it, it pisses me off.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.990
It's so embarrassing when they're the ones representing Japan!

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.510
Why?!

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:29.840
Isn't that team...?

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:30.630
Yeah.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.490
It's Protocol Omega.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:37.650
They've switched places with the real Japan representatives and messed up the game.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.320
What do you mean?

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:42.340
This match is an Interruption point.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:44.390
I-Interruption?

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:46.010
Interruption point...

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.890
The fork in the road of destiny.

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.760
Huh?

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.000
From this match, history changed.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.330
You're really quick on the uptake...

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:00.280
But why are our memories different from everyone else's?

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:08.280
That's due to whether you were inside or outside of the history that's been meddled with.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.530
Who are you?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.740
Doctor Aruno!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.800
Why are you here?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.560
El Dorado was closing in on me.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.660
I used space-time to make a lickety-split.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.450
Meaning I ran away as fast as I could.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:25.030
Are we okay?

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.280
I make no slip-ups.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:33.680
My pursuer should be lost within the wormhole right about now.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:34.510
Who's he?

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:35.360
No idea...

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.930
Allow me to introduce you!

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:39.810
This man is the one and only!

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:45.180
The big scientist who proposed a theory on multiple timelines and is the inventor of the time machine...

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.210
Doctor Crossword Aruno!

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.750
At this point...

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.450
I just have no idea what's going on.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.530
Amazing!

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.950
I got to meet a scientist from the future!

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.560
This is perfect.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:05.850
Let's use this opportunity to hear from the doctor himself on his multiple timeline theory.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.740
Okay, I'm ready.

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:16.230
I've linked video clip data from within my library to this monitor.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.220
Now, let me begin.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:24.430
By nature, there is only one path that the flow of time travels along.

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.280
However, when history is changed, much like what is happening right now,

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:31.260
it can create a new flow of time, which we call a parallel world.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:37.200
Depending on the time, there are situations when more than one parallel world can be made.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:40.480
It's like what happened with Tsurugi's brother.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:44.560
But the Yuuichi-san who fought with us turned back to normal.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:47.080
What do you mean?

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:50.410
We'll tell you more about it some other day.

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:55.010
The parallel worlds have another particular trait that is very significant.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:59.730
Although the history that has been changed show a multiple number of lines temporarily,

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.140
it gradually but steadily returns to one.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.840
All timelines besides the one that has been rendered genuine will eventually disappear.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:10.520
Kind of like a guitar string that's been plucked.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:14.070
Guitar?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:20.530
Because Tenma-kun and those who have time jumped were in a different but concurrently flowing timeline,

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.040
they were not affected when the timeline here was meddled with.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:28.410
That is why you still have memories of what really happened one month ago.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:34.920
So if we don't do something, the soccer ban will become a real part of history.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.560
Exactly!

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:38.780
You're a pretty smart girl!

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:41.600
So that's it...

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:46.940
So if we don't do something, we'll lose our future.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.020
This is too difficult for me!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.060
So, to sum it up, what do we do?!

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.700
It's very simple.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:59.550
You must time jump to the Interruption point before the changes in history grow fixed.

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:01.750
Yes, and...

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:06.180
Through our efforts, we will stop El Dorado!

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:11.960
So we're going to the point in time before the match between Japan and America began?

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.100
Yes.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:17.240
We'll switch with America's team and fight Protocol Omega.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.030
We're going to time jump, too?

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.630
This is getting big.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:24.670
I'm going!

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:27.100
Let's go get soccer back.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.260
I don't want a world where there's no soccer.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:30.600
You're right.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.370
Okay then, let's try it.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.820
We must endeavor to take back our own future.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:37.670
That's the spirit!

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:41.870
And you have the great Coach Wondeba-sama alongside you for support.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.390
There is nothing to fear.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:46.650
Coach Endou! Please lead us!

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.580
Raimon's coach has gotta be Coach Endou.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:56.790
Fei, I want you to join us as a member.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:58.260
Okay!

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:01.920
I'm glad to see you all fired up, but do you have an Artifact?

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.380
Artifact?

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:05.580
We need it to make the time jump.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:10.190
It can be anything as long as it's connected to the Interruption point.

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.780
Like a soccer ball or a uniform.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.480
Oh yeah!

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.540
How's this?

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.530
I kept the ticket stub of that match.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.670
Yeah, that should work!

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.580
Right, Doctor Aruno?

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.410
Huh? He's gone.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.720
The doctor is, after all, a busy man.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.960
That's not the issue...

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.010
It's flying...

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:46.710
Now then, let's go!

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.970
T minus 5 seconds to time jump!

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.270
4...

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.370
3...

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:52.430
2...

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:53.400
1...

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.400
Time jump!

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:00.880
It disappeared...

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:05.290
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.540
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.650
So this is a time jump.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.440
This feels so weird...

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:24.240
We pass through wormholes to get to the past.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:25.470
Wormhole?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.850
It's like a tunnel connecting space-time to space-time.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:31.840
Did you get that?

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.050
N-No...

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.730
So this is a wormhole...

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.900
What's wrong, Akane?!

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.210
Akane-san?!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:43.530
It won't show up.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.480
D-Don't scare me like that...

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:55.080
It looks like the game has already started.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.610
Are we too late?

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.580
No, the game isn't over yet.

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:02.020
Let's go!

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:02.800
Yes, sir!

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:06.180
Goal!

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:10.680
Japan's representatives show overwhelming power as they take their eighth point!

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.280
This is...

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.010
It really is horrible.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.710
This is the sort of match that Protocol Omega plays?

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:28.500
Why is everyone keeping quiet and letting this match go on?

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.820
Look up there.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.080
A ball?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.580
It's the Sphere device!

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:39.960
They're using that to brainwash everyone.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:46.030
So that's why no one is noticing that there's something wrong?

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:49.180
I knew you would come.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.930
Protocol Omega!

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:55.340
We won't let this game go the way you want it to!

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.770
Wondeba-san and Fei-san, I presume?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.410
You've got that right.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:00.560
And you are?

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:02.290
I'm Beta.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.020
What happened to Alpha?

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:05.490
Well...

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:09.110
I suppose this is what you call "getting sacked"?

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.490
Such a pity.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.490
Protocol Omega has fallen.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.870
This is most deplorable.

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.580
I apologize.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:24.420
We have analyzed the cause of your defeat and have made a decision.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.420
Netan, Genie, Kual...

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:32.430
...and Alpha are dismissed and will be sent to Infinity Prison.

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:34.390
No!

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:35.830
Please wait!

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:37.840
We will answer to your expectations next time!

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.480
Go.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.820
Chairman!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.150
Additional members will be replacing them.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:49.910
Ward.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:51.000
Orca.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.070
Drim.

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.660
And Beta.

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:57.250
Yes, sir.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.670
You will lead the team in Alpha's place.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.380
Understood.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.970
We're Protocol Omega 2.0.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:08.650
A version upgrade.

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:11.490
Who cares which one you are, let's fight!

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:13.380
We're taking back soccer!

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.520
Very well.

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:20.890
But I doubt that you are strong enough to beat us.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.030
This friendly between Japan and America is full of ups and downs.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.440
What more will happen after this?

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.860
Huh? What's going on?

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.330
There's something weird going on down at the field.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.950
Just what is about to happen?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.350
Let me ask you again.

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.330
Do you really want to fight with us?

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.900
Of course!

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:46.420
We'll win no matter what!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.770
I don't think you should even bother trying.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:51.630
But as you wish.

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:55.040
Now, the game resumes!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:58.260
America's representatives have allowed a large point difference to Japan's representatives.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:01.360
Will they be able to rally from here on?

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:06.090
I've inputted your data into the commentator's brain.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:09.980
Now you are America's representatives.

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:17.330
Call Mode.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.700
Well, let's begin.

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.120
Both teams are back in position!

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:28.360
The match resumes with a kickoff by America!

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:29.700
Let's go!

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.080
There's the kickoff!

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:36.110
Tsurugi! Watch out for rough plays!

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.380
Drim, go get him.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:43.390
Tsurugi!

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:46.770
Japan's Drim steals the ball!

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.290
Are you okay?

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.350
Yeah.

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:51.150
You think you can do whatever you want?

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:52.800
That's right!

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:54.340
I won't let you!

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:04.540
Wonder Trap!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.520
Good one, Tenma!

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.500
A new hissatsu technique!

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:10.420
Tenma!

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.250
Okay!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.090
Shindou-senpai!

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:16.950
America's representatives make sharp passes!

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:19.450
The ball goes from Matsukaze to Shindou, to Fei...

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.830
And Nishiki is unmarked!

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.940
Leave this to me!

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.610
Sengoku War God Musashi!

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:41.660
Bushin Renzan!

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.770
Zanou, go for it.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:52.160
What?

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.270
He stops it!

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:57.310
He uses his body to stop the Avatar shoot!

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.900
That's insane...

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:01.400
How can Avatar shoots not work?

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:05.170
Your Avatars are useless!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.660
I'll compliment you for even being able to make a shoot.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.330
But that's as far as you'll get.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.350
Now it's our turn!

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:12.820
Orca!

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:13.980
Okay!

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.610
Now, Japan's representatives counterattack!

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:17.420
Out of my way!

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:23.530
Medam!

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:24.640
A back pass?

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.750
Japan's team uses skillful passwork!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.170
This time they close in on America's goal!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:31.320
Not good!

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.570
Kirino! Amagi-san!

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.630
Oh no!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.280
Thank you, Drim.

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:44.080
Come out!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:48.270
Goddess of the Vacant Skies...

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.040
Athena!

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:52.750
Armed!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.150
Sangoku-senpai!

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:08.950
Right!

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:12.520
Unassisted Hand!

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:16.950
Goal!

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:19.750
Japan makes another goal!

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:27.560
W-What was that?

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.940
She wore her Avatar...

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.960
That's Avatar Armed.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.400
What is that?

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.140
You turn your Avatar into armor and equip yourself with it.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:38.650
It rapidly raises your abilities.

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:42.770
Will Tenma and the others be okay against that?

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:46.260
Tenma has been able to perform Avatar Armed before.

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.010
Tenma can do that too?!

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:52.210
That's awesome! He's progressing!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.110
Yes. He's managed to pull it off, but...

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:56.640
What?

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:58.280
Is there something wrong?

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:06.870
Now, will America's team be able to face off against the momentum of Japan's team?!

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:09.790
If I can do it again, like last time...

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:12.310
<i>Armed!</i>

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.300
Fei!

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:26.700
Shindou-kun!

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:27.680
Tenma!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:29.740
All right!

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.350
Go, Tenma!

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:42.340
Demon God Pegasus Arc!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:44.990
Armed!

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:57.860
I can't use Avatar Armed!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.350
Boohoo for you.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:04.330
Matsukaze has the ball stolen from him just when he was about to shoot!

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:06.530
Why...

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:08.660
I was able to do it before...

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.230
Tenma, you okay?

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:12.340
Y-Yeah!

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.160
I knew it...

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:26.210
Why can't I use Avatar Armed?

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:57.310
This is really bad! I can't use Avatar Armed!

00:22:57.310 --> 00:22:59.850
What's more, an even more shocking situation presses in on Raimon!

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:04.150
Next, Fierce! Protocol Omega 2.0!!

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:05.900
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:18.650
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:22.220 --> 00:23:26.020
We must endeavor to take back our own future!

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:27.190
That's all!
